IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-dates`

-- Sex Discrimination Act 1984 (Cth) -- harassment at work and the positive duty, from the seat of the person it happens to.
--
-- SEAT: the employee, worker or job seeker on the receiving end of the conduct. "Was I sexually harassed? Is it unlawful?
-- Does my employer have to do something about it? Is my employer liable for what my colleague did? Can I complain, and by
-- when? Will I have to pay costs if I lose?" Every question is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person
-- could state; the judgments the Act leaves to the Commission or a court are inputs.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Sexual harassment (s 28A); harassment on the ground of sex (s 28AA, with s 8); worker in a business
-- or undertaking (s 28AB); harassment in employment and work (s 28B(1)-(8)); hostile workplace environments (s 28M, with
-- s 8A); victimisation (s 47A, with the (3) defence) and the offence (s 94); the positive duty (Part IIA: ss 47B, 47C);
-- liability of persons involved (s 105); vicarious liability (s 106); no right of action for Part IIA (s 110). From the
-- Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986: "unlawful discrimination" (s 3(1)(c)), lodging a complaint (s 46P), late
-- lodging (s 46PH(1)(b)), the 60 days to go to court (s 46PO(2)) and costs (s 46PSA).
--
-- Edition: Compilation date 1 November 2025 (includes amendments up to Act No. 45, 2025; register id C2025C00597), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A02868.txt. Also used: Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986,
-- Compilation No. 58, compilation date 18 September 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 87, 2026; register id
-- C2026C00416), as deposited at
-- ../../../australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986/registers/source-bundle/C2004A03366.txt -- ss 3(1), 46P, 46PH(1)(b),
-- 46PO(2), 46PSA only. No regulations set a number this encoding needs.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Sex discrimination itself (ss 5-7B, 14-27: an input where s 47C(2)(a) and s 106(1)(a) need it); the other
-- areas of harassment (ss 28C-28L); the exemptions (Part II Division 4); the Commission's positive-duty powers (AHRC Act
-- Division 4A: inquiries, compliance notices, undertakings), which are the duty holder's to meet; the President's inquiry
-- and conciliation; remedies; the constitutional reach (s 9: assumed); penalty unit values (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA).
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Sex Discrimination Act 1984 -- harassment at work and the positive duty`

-- Who did the conduct, as it relates to the organisation the questions are about (the employer or the business).
DECLARE `Who did it` IS ONE OF
    `the organisation itself`
    `an employee of the organisation`
    `a worker in the business`
    `an agent of the organisation`
    `someone else`

-- The facts of one piece of conduct towards one person, as that person can state them. Built inside each question from
-- plain inputs; see the @desc of each input on the exported questions for what it asks.
DECLARE Facts HAS
    `conduct date` IS A DATE
    `org employs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `org is a PCBU` IS A BOOLEAN
    `me employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `me worker` IS A BOOLEAN
    `me seeking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `actor` IS A `Who did it`
    `connected with my work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `connected with their work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sexual advance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sexual conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `demeaning conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sex a reason` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable person offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in my workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in their workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
    `present` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable person hostile` IS A BOOLEAN
    `work discrimination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `victimised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `false allegation proved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `raised covered conduct` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN c IS A BOOLEAN, s IS A STRING, rest IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`with if` c s rest MEANS
    IF c THEN s FOLLOWED BY rest ELSE rest

§§ `ss 28A, 28AA, 8 -- was I harassed`

-- s 28A(1): "a person sexually harasses another person (the person harassed) if: (a) the person makes an unwelcome sexual
-- advance, or an unwelcome request for sexual favours, to the person harassed; or (b) engages in other unwelcome conduct
-- of a sexual nature in relation to the person harassed; in circumstances in which a reasonable person, having regard to
-- all the circumstances, would have anticipated the possibility that the person harassed would be offended, humiliated or
-- intimidated." (2): conduct of a sexual nature "includes making a statement of a sexual nature to a person, or in the
-- presence of a person, whether the statement is made orally or in writing."
-- Plain gloss: unwelcome sexual behaviour that a reasonable person would have seen might offend, humiliate or intimidate.
GIVEN f IS A Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sexually harassed` f IF
        (f's `sexual advance` OR f's `sexual conduct`)
    AND f's `reasonable person offence`

-- s 28AA(1): a person harasses another "on the ground of sex if: (a) by reason of: (i) the sex of the person harassed; or
-- (ii) a characteristic that appertains generally to persons of the sex of the person harassed; or (iii) a characteristic
-- that is generally imputed to persons of the sex of the person harassed; the person engages in unwelcome conduct of a
-- demeaning nature in relation to the person harassed; and (b) ... a reasonable person ... would have anticipated the
-- possibility that the person harassed would be offended, humiliated or intimidated." s 8: the reason need only be one of
-- 2 or more, "whether or not ... the dominant or substantial reason".
-- Plain gloss: demeaning behaviour aimed at you because of your sex (or what is assumed of your sex).
GIVEN f IS A Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `harassed on the ground of sex` f IF
        f's `demeaning conduct`
    AND f's `sex a reason`
    AND f's `reasonable person offence`

GIVEN f IS A Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `harassed` f IF `sexually harassed` f OR `harassed on the ground of sex` f

@export Was I sexually harassed (s 28A)?
GIVEN `unwelcome sexual advance or request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was an unwelcome sexual advance, or an unwelcome request for sexual favours, made to you
      `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature towards you, including a statement of a sexual nature made to you or in your presence, spoken or written
      `a reasonable person would anticipate offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances (your sex, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, intersex status, relationship status, religion, race, disability, your relationship with them, anything else relevant), would have anticipated the possibility that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated (a judgment for the Commission or court)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I sexually harassed` IF
        (`unwelcome sexual advance or request` OR `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature`)
    AND `a reasonable person would anticipate offence`

@export Was I harassed on the ground of my sex (ss 28AA, 8)?
GIVEN `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature towards you, including a statement made to you or in your presence
      `my sex was one of the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your sex, or a characteristic generally belonging to or assumed of people of your sex, was a reason for it, even if not the main reason
      `a reasonable person would anticipate offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances (including any power imbalance, how serious it was and whether it was repeated), would have anticipated the possibility that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated (a judgment for the Commission or court)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I harassed on the ground of my sex` IF
        `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature`
    AND `my sex was one of the reasons`
    AND `a reasonable person would anticipate offence`

§§ `ss 28M, 8A -- was my workplace made hostile on the ground of sex`

-- s 28M(1): "It is unlawful for a person to subject another person to a workplace environment that is hostile on the
-- ground of sex." (2): that happens if "(a) the first person engages in conduct in a workplace where the first person or
-- the second person, or both, work; and (b) the second person is in the workplace at the same time as or after the
-- conduct occurs; and (c) a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances, would have anticipated the
-- possibility of the conduct resulting in the workplace environment being offensive, intimidating or humiliating to a
-- person of the sex of the second person by reason of" the sex or a characteristic of that sex. s 8A: one of 2 or more
-- reasons is enough. s 28M was added by Act No. 85, 2022, from 13 December 2022 (see `sda-dates`); conduct before then
-- is not unlawful under it.
-- Plain gloss: conduct at work (posters, jokes, talk) that a reasonable person would see could make the place
-- offensive, intimidating or humiliating for people of your sex -- it need not be aimed at you.
GIVEN f IS A Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subjected to a hostile workplace environment` f IF
        f's `conduct date` AT LEAST `Respect at Work 2022 commencement`
    AND (f's `in my workplace` OR f's `in their workplace`)
    AND f's `present`
    AND f's `reasonable person hostile`

@export Was I subjected to a workplace environment hostile on the ground of my sex (ss 28M, 8A)?
GIVEN `date of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct happened (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-15); s 28M applies from 13 December 2022
      `it was in a workplace where I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where you work
      `it was in a workplace where they work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where the person who did it works
      `I was there at the time or after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in that workplace at the same time as the conduct or after it
      `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances (seriousness, whether continuous or repeated, the role or authority of the person), would have anticipated the possibility of the conduct making the workplace offensive, intimidating or humiliating to a person of your sex because of sex or a characteristic of that sex, even as one of several reasons (a judgment for the Commission or court)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I subjected to a hostile workplace environment` IF
        `date of the conduct` AT LEAST `Respect at Work 2022 commencement`
    AND (`it was in a workplace where I work` OR `it was in a workplace where they work`)
    AND `I was there at the time or after`
    AND `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment`

§§ `ss 28AB, 28B -- is the harassment unlawful at work`

-- s 28B: "It is unlawful" for --
-- (1) a person to harass "(a) an employee of the person; or (b) a person who is seeking to become an employee of the
--     person";
-- (2) "an employee to ... harass ... a fellow employee or a person who is seeking employment with the same employer";
-- (3) "a person conducting a business or undertaking to ... harass ... (a) a worker in the business or undertaking; or
--     (b) a person who is seeking to become a worker in the business or undertaking";
-- (4) "a worker in a business or undertaking to ... harass ... (a) a fellow worker; or (b) a person who is seeking to
--     become a worker in the business or undertaking";
-- (5), (7) a worker, a person conducting a business or undertaking, an employee or an employer to harass "a person if
--     the harassment occurs in connection with the first person being" one;
-- (6), (8) a person to harass a worker, a person conducting a business or undertaking, an employee or an employer "if the
--     harassment occurs in connection with the second person being" one.
-- s 28AB: a person who carries out work for a person conducting a business or undertaking is "a worker in the business
-- or undertaking". "worker" and "person conducting a business or undertaking" have their Work Health and Safety Act 2011
-- meaning (s 4): asked as facts.
-- Read here: "harass" covers both sexual harassment and harassment on the ground of sex, as every subsection says.
-- An employee of the organisation is treated under (2); a worker who is not its employee under (4). Whether an employee
-- is also a "worker" (WHS Act s 7) is a borrowed term this encoding does not decide for the person who did it.
GIVEN f IS A Facts
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 28B subsections` f MEANS
    IF NOT (`harassed` f)
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE `with if` `sub 1` "s 28B(1)"
          (`with if` `sub 2` "s 28B(2)"
            (`with if` `sub 3` "s 28B(3)"
              (`with if` `sub 4` "s 28B(4)"
                (`with if` (f's `connected with their work`) "s 28B(5) or (7)"
                  (`with if` (f's `connected with my work`) "s 28B(6) or (8)"
                    EMPTY)))))
    WHERE
        `sub 1` MEANS `it is the organisation itself` AND f's `org employs` AND (f's `me employee` OR f's `me seeking`)
        `sub 2` MEANS `it is an employee` AND f's `org employs` AND (f's `me employee` OR f's `me seeking`)
        `sub 3` MEANS `it is the organisation itself` AND f's `org is a PCBU` AND (f's `me worker` OR f's `me seeking`)
        `sub 4` MEANS `it is a worker` AND f's `org is a PCBU` AND (f's `me worker` OR f's `me seeking`)
        `it is the organisation itself` MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `actor`
            WHEN `the organisation itself` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `it is an employee` MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `actor`
            WHEN `an employee of the organisation` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `it is a worker` MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `actor`
            WHEN `a worker in the business` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN f IS A Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `harassment unlawful under s 28B` f IF NOT (null (`s 28B subsections` f))

-- s 28B lists situations without closing the list with "only", and ss 28C-28L make harassment unlawful in other areas
-- (not encoded). So: no harassment at all (ss 28A, 28AA are "if" definitions) -> JUST FALSE; harassment in a s 28B
-- situation -> JUST TRUE; harassment outside every s 28B situation -> NOTHING (this section does not say).
GIVEN f IS A Facts
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28B answer` f MEANS
    IF NOT (`harassed` f) THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `harassment unlawful under s 28B` f
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

@export Is the sexual harassment, or harassment on the ground of sex, I suffered unlawful under s 28B (employment and work)?
GIVEN `date of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct happened (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-15)
      `the organisation is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation you are asking about employs people (it may be your employer or someone else's)
      `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is a person conducting a business or undertaking (a PCBU, as in the Work Health and Safety Act 2011)
      `I am an employee of the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed by the organisation
      `I am a worker in the business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carry out work for the organisation's business or undertaking in any capacity (employee, contractor, labour hire, apprentice, volunteer and so on)
      `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were applying or seeking to become an employee of, or a worker in, the organisation
      `who did it` IS A `Who did it` @desc Who did the conduct, as it relates to the organisation: the organisation itself, one of its employees, a worker in its business, one of its agents, or someone else (a customer, client, member of the public, another business's worker)
      `it was connected with my being an employee or worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in connection with your being an employee or a worker (for example at work, at a work event, or because of your work)
      `they acted in connection with their own work or business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who did it is an employee, employer, worker or person conducting a business and did it in connection with being one
      `unwelcome sexual advance or request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was an unwelcome sexual advance, or an unwelcome request for sexual favours, made to you
      `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature towards you, including a statement of a sexual nature made to you or in your presence, spoken or written
      `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature towards you, including a statement made to you or in your presence
      `my sex was one of the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your sex, or a characteristic generally belonging to or assumed of people of your sex, was a reason for the demeaning conduct, even if not the main reason (s 8)
      `a reasonable person would anticipate offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances, would have anticipated the possibility that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated (a judgment for the Commission or court; answer as you expect it to be found)
      `it was in a workplace where I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where you work
      `it was in a workplace where they work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where the person who did it works
      `I was there at the time or after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in that workplace at the same time as the conduct or after it
      `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances (seriousness, repetition, the role or authority of the person), would have anticipated the possibility of the conduct making the workplace offensive, intimidating or humiliating to a person of your sex because of sex or a characteristic of that sex, even as one of several reasons (a judgment for the Commission or court)
      `it was sex discrimination in work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was discrimination against you on the ground of your sex that is unlawful under s 14(1) or (2), 15, 16 or 17 (employment, commission agents, contract workers, partnerships); not worked out in this encoding
      `I suffered detriment for speaking up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were subjected to, or threatened with, a detriment because you complained, brought proceedings, gave information, attended a conference, were a witness, asserted rights or made an allegation under the Act (or because they believed you had or would)
      `the false allegation defence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reason for the detriment was an allegation you made, and it has been proved that the allegation was false and not made in good faith (s 47A(3))
      `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you complained of, asserted or alleged was sex discrimination in work, sexual harassment or harassment on the ground of sex at work, or a hostile workplace environment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the harassment of me unlawful under section 28B` MEANS `s 28B answer` `the facts`
    WHERE
    `the facts` MEANS Facts WITH `conduct date` IS `date of the conduct`
                                 `org employs` IS `the organisation is an employer`
                                 `org is a PCBU` IS `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking`
                                 `me employee` IS `I am an employee of the organisation`
                                 `me worker` IS `I am a worker in the business or undertaking`
                                 `me seeking` IS `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there`
                                 `actor` IS `who did it`
                                 `connected with my work` IS `it was connected with my being an employee or worker`
                                 `connected with their work` IS `they acted in connection with their own work or business`
                                 `sexual advance` IS `unwelcome sexual advance or request`
                                 `sexual conduct` IS `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature`
                                 `demeaning conduct` IS `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature`
                                 `sex a reason` IS `my sex was one of the reasons`
                                 `reasonable person offence` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate offence`
                                 `in my workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where I work`
                                 `in their workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where they work`
                                 `present` IS `I was there at the time or after`
                                 `reasonable person hostile` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment`
                                 `work discrimination` IS `it was sex discrimination in work`
                                 `victimised` IS `I suffered detriment for speaking up`
                                 `false allegation proved` IS `the false allegation defence is proved`
                                 `raised covered conduct` IS `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace`

@export Which subsections of s 28B make the harassment I suffered unlawful?
GIVEN `date of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct happened (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-15)
      `the organisation is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation you are asking about employs people (it may be your employer or someone else's)
      `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is a person conducting a business or undertaking (a PCBU, as in the Work Health and Safety Act 2011)
      `I am an employee of the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed by the organisation
      `I am a worker in the business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carry out work for the organisation's business or undertaking in any capacity (employee, contractor, labour hire, apprentice, volunteer and so on)
      `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were applying or seeking to become an employee of, or a worker in, the organisation
      `who did it` IS A `Who did it` @desc Who did the conduct, as it relates to the organisation: the organisation itself, one of its employees, a worker in its business, one of its agents, or someone else (a customer, client, member of the public, another business's worker)
      `it was connected with my being an employee or worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in connection with your being an employee or a worker (for example at work, at a work event, or because of your work)
      `they acted in connection with their own work or business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who did it is an employee, employer, worker or person conducting a business and did it in connection with being one
      `unwelcome sexual advance or request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was an unwelcome sexual advance, or an unwelcome request for sexual favours, made to you
      `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature towards you, including a statement of a sexual nature made to you or in your presence, spoken or written
      `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature towards you, including a statement made to you or in your presence
      `my sex was one of the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your sex, or a characteristic generally belonging to or assumed of people of your sex, was a reason for the demeaning conduct, even if not the main reason (s 8)
      `a reasonable person would anticipate offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances, would have anticipated the possibility that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated (a judgment for the Commission or court; answer as you expect it to be found)
      `it was in a workplace where I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where you work
      `it was in a workplace where they work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where the person who did it works
      `I was there at the time or after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in that workplace at the same time as the conduct or after it
      `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances (seriousness, repetition, the role or authority of the person), would have anticipated the possibility of the conduct making the workplace offensive, intimidating or humiliating to a person of your sex because of sex or a characteristic of that sex, even as one of several reasons (a judgment for the Commission or court)
      `it was sex discrimination in work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was discrimination against you on the ground of your sex that is unlawful under s 14(1) or (2), 15, 16 or 17 (employment, commission agents, contract workers, partnerships); not worked out in this encoding
      `I suffered detriment for speaking up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were subjected to, or threatened with, a detriment because you complained, brought proceedings, gave information, attended a conference, were a witness, asserted rights or made an allegation under the Act (or because they believed you had or would)
      `the false allegation defence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reason for the detriment was an allegation you made, and it has been proved that the allegation was false and not made in good faith (s 47A(3))
      `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you complained of, asserted or alleged was sex discrimination in work, sexual harassment or harassment on the ground of sex at work, or a hostile workplace environment
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Which subsections of section 28B make the harassment of me unlawful` MEANS `s 28B subsections` `the facts`
    WHERE
    `the facts` MEANS Facts WITH `conduct date` IS `date of the conduct`
                                 `org employs` IS `the organisation is an employer`
                                 `org is a PCBU` IS `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking`
                                 `me employee` IS `I am an employee of the organisation`
                                 `me worker` IS `I am a worker in the business or undertaking`
                                 `me seeking` IS `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there`
                                 `actor` IS `who did it`
                                 `connected with my work` IS `it was connected with my being an employee or worker`
                                 `connected with their work` IS `they acted in connection with their own work or business`
                                 `sexual advance` IS `unwelcome sexual advance or request`
                                 `sexual conduct` IS `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature`
                                 `demeaning conduct` IS `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature`
                                 `sex a reason` IS `my sex was one of the reasons`
                                 `reasonable person offence` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate offence`
                                 `in my workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where I work`
                                 `in their workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where they work`
                                 `present` IS `I was there at the time or after`
                                 `reasonable person hostile` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment`
                                 `work discrimination` IS `it was sex discrimination in work`
                                 `victimised` IS `I suffered detriment for speaking up`
                                 `false allegation proved` IS `the false allegation defence is proved`
                                 `raised covered conduct` IS `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace`

§§ `ss 47A, 94 -- was I victimised for speaking up`

-- s 47A(1): "It is unlawful for a person to commit an act of victimisation against another person." (2): a person
-- commits one if they subject, "or threaten to subject, the other person to any detriment on the ground that the other
-- person" has made or proposes to make a complaint, brought proceedings, given information, attended a conference,
-- appeared as a witness, "reasonably asserted ... any rights", or alleged unlawful conduct under Part II or a contravention
-- of Part IIA, or on the ground that they believe the other person has done or proposes to do any of these.
-- (3): "In a proceeding for a contravention of subsection (1) constituted by subjecting, or threatening to subject, a
-- person to a detriment on the ground that the person has made an allegation mentioned in paragraph (2)(g) or (h), it is a
-- defence if it is proved that the allegation was false and was not made in good faith."
DECLARE `Victimisation answer` IS ONE OF
    `victimisation, unlawful under s 47A`
    `the s 47A(3) defence applies: the allegation was false and not made in good faith`
    `not victimisation under s 47A`

GIVEN f IS A Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `victimisation unlawful` f IF f's `victimised` AND (NOT f's `false allegation proved`)

@export Was I victimised for complaining, or for asserting my rights, under the Sex Discrimination Act (s 47A)?
GIVEN `I suffered detriment for speaking up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were subjected to, or threatened with, a detriment because you complained, brought proceedings, gave information, attended a conference, were a witness, asserted rights or made an allegation under the Act or the Australian Human Rights Commission Act (or because they believed you had or would)
      `the false allegation defence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reason for the detriment was an allegation you made, and it has been proved that the allegation was false and not made in good faith
GIVETH A `Victimisation answer`
`Was I victimised` MEANS
    IF NOT `I suffered detriment for speaking up` THEN `not victimisation under s 47A`
    ELSE IF `the false allegation defence is proved`
         THEN `the s 47A(3) defence applies: the allegation was false and not made in good faith`
         ELSE `victimisation, unlawful under s 47A`

-- s 94(1): "A person shall not commit an act of victimisation against another person. Penalty: (a) in the case of a
-- natural person--25 penalty units or imprisonment for 3 months, or both; or (b) in the case of a body corporate--100
-- penalty units." The value of a penalty unit is set by the Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, not deposited: the answer is in
-- penalty units.
@export What is the most the person who victimised me can be fined, in penalty units (s 94)?
GIVEN `they are a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who victimised you is a company or other body corporate (rather than an individual)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most they can be fined in penalty units` MEANS
    IF `they are a body corporate` THEN 100 ELSE 25

@export What is the longest the person who victimised me can be imprisoned, in months (s 94)? 0 means the Act gives no imprisonment.
GIVEN `they are a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who victimised you is a company or other body corporate (rather than an individual)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the longest they can be imprisoned in months` MEANS
    IF `they are a body corporate` THEN 0 ELSE 3

§§ `Part IIA, ss 47B, 47C -- must the organisation act to eliminate this conduct`

-- s 47C(1): "An employer or a person conducting a business or undertaking (the duty holder) must take reasonable and
-- proportionate measures to eliminate, as far as possible: (a) conduct covered by subsection (2) by persons covered by
-- subsection (3); and (b) conduct covered by subsection (4)."
-- (2): "(a) discrimination on the ground of a person's sex that is unlawful under ... subsection 14(1) or (2) ... section
-- 15 ... section 16 ... section 17; (b) sexual harassment, or harassment on the ground of sex, that is unlawful under
-- section 28B; (c) conduct that is unlawful under section 28M (hostile workplace environments); (d) acts of victimisation
-- (within the meaning of section 47A) that relate to complaints, proceedings, assertions or allegations in relation to
-- conduct mentioned in any of paragraphs (a) to (c)".
-- (3): "(a) the duty holder; (b) if the duty holder is an employer--the duty holder's employees; (c) if the duty holder is
-- a person conducting a business or undertaking--workers in the business or undertaking; (d) the duty holder's agents."
-- (4): "(a) sexual harassment, or harassment on the ground of sex, of persons covered by subsection (5) that is unlawful
-- under subsection 28B(6) or (8); (b) conduct in workplaces where persons covered by subsection (5) work that is unlawful
-- under section 28M ...; (c) acts of victimisation (within the meaning of section 47A) against persons covered by
-- subsection (5) that relate to" such complaints and so on.
-- (5): "(a) if the duty holder is an employer--the duty holder's employees; (b) if the duty holder is a person conducting
-- a business or undertaking--workers in the business or undertaking."
-- (6): compliance takes into account size, nature and circumstances, resources, practicability and cost, and any other
-- relevant matter. Compliance is a judgment for the Commission (AHRC Act Division 4A) and is not encoded.
-- Part IIA was added by Act No. 85, 2022, from 13 December 2022 (see `sda-dates`).
-- Plain gloss: from 13 December 2022 your employer (or the business you work in) must take reasonable and proportionate
-- steps to stamp out sex discrimination, sexual and sex-based harassment, hostile workplaces and victimisation -- by itself
-- and its people, and by anyone (customers, clients, visitors) towards its own employees and workers.
GIVEN f IS A Facts
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 47C paragraphs` f MEANS
    IF NOT (`is a duty holder` AND f's `conduct date` AT LEAST `Respect at Work 2022 commencement`)
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE `with if` (`by a subsection (3) person` AND f's `work discrimination`) `text 2a`
          (`with if` (`by a subsection (3) person` AND `harassment unlawful under s 28B` f) `text 2b`
            (`with if` (`by a subsection (3) person` AND `subjected to a hostile workplace environment` f) `text 2c`
              (`with if` (`by a subsection (3) person` AND `victimisation about covered conduct`) `text 2d`
                (`with if` (`I am a subsection (5) person` AND `harassed` f AND f's `connected with my work`) `text 4a`
                  (`with if` (`I am a subsection (5) person` AND f's `in my workplace` AND `subjected to a hostile workplace environment` f) `text 4b`
                    (`with if` (`I am a subsection (5) person` AND `victimisation about covered conduct`) `text 4c`
                      EMPTY))))))
    WHERE
        `text 2a` MEANS "s 47C(1)(a), (2)(a): sex discrimination in work by the duty holder, its employees, workers or agents"
        `text 2b` MEANS "s 47C(1)(a), (2)(b): harassment unlawful under s 28B by the duty holder, its employees, workers or agents"
        `text 2c` MEANS "s 47C(1)(a), (2)(c): a hostile workplace environment (s 28M) created by the duty holder, its employees, workers or agents"
        `text 2d` MEANS "s 47C(1)(a), (2)(d): victimisation about such conduct by the duty holder, its employees, workers or agents"
        `text 4a` MEANS "s 47C(1)(b), (4)(a): harassment of its employees or workers unlawful under s 28B(6) or (8)"
        `text 4b` MEANS "s 47C(1)(b), (4)(b): a hostile workplace environment (s 28M) in a workplace where its employees or workers work"
        `text 4c` MEANS "s 47C(1)(b), (4)(c): victimisation of its employees or workers about such conduct"
        `is a duty holder` MEANS f's `org employs` OR f's `org is a PCBU`
        `by a subsection (3) person` MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `actor`
            WHEN `the organisation itself` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an employee of the organisation` THEN f's `org employs`
            WHEN `a worker in the business` THEN f's `org is a PCBU`
            WHEN `an agent of the organisation` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `I am a subsection (5) person` MEANS
                (f's `org employs` AND f's `me employee`)
            OR (f's `org is a PCBU` AND f's `me worker`)
        -- (2)(d), (4)(c) say "acts of victimisation (within the meaning of section 47A)", not "unlawful under": the s 47A(3)
        -- defence, which operates "in a proceeding", is not read into them (finding 6).
        `victimisation about covered conduct` MEANS f's `victimised` AND f's `raised covered conduct`

-- s 47C(1) defines its reach by subsections that say "this subsection covers the following" conduct and persons: read as
-- closed lists, so conduct outside them is JUST FALSE (fork F1: the other reading is NOTHING).
GIVEN f IS A Facts
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47C answer` f MEANS
    IF null (`s 47C paragraphs` f) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

@export Does the positive duty (s 47C) require my employer, or the business I work in, to take reasonable and proportionate measures to eliminate this conduct?
GIVEN `date of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct happened (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-15)
      `the organisation is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation you are asking about employs people (it may be your employer or someone else's)
      `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is a person conducting a business or undertaking (a PCBU, as in the Work Health and Safety Act 2011)
      `I am an employee of the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed by the organisation
      `I am a worker in the business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carry out work for the organisation's business or undertaking in any capacity (employee, contractor, labour hire, apprentice, volunteer and so on)
      `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were applying or seeking to become an employee of, or a worker in, the organisation
      `who did it` IS A `Who did it` @desc Who did the conduct, as it relates to the organisation: the organisation itself, one of its employees, a worker in its business, one of its agents, or someone else (a customer, client, member of the public, another business's worker)
      `it was connected with my being an employee or worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in connection with your being an employee or a worker (for example at work, at a work event, or because of your work)
      `they acted in connection with their own work or business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who did it is an employee, employer, worker or person conducting a business and did it in connection with being one
      `unwelcome sexual advance or request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was an unwelcome sexual advance, or an unwelcome request for sexual favours, made to you
      `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature towards you, including a statement of a sexual nature made to you or in your presence, spoken or written
      `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature towards you, including a statement made to you or in your presence
      `my sex was one of the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your sex, or a characteristic generally belonging to or assumed of people of your sex, was a reason for the demeaning conduct, even if not the main reason (s 8)
      `a reasonable person would anticipate offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances, would have anticipated the possibility that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated (a judgment for the Commission or court; answer as you expect it to be found)
      `it was in a workplace where I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where you work
      `it was in a workplace where they work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where the person who did it works
      `I was there at the time or after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in that workplace at the same time as the conduct or after it
      `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances (seriousness, repetition, the role or authority of the person), would have anticipated the possibility of the conduct making the workplace offensive, intimidating or humiliating to a person of your sex because of sex or a characteristic of that sex, even as one of several reasons (a judgment for the Commission or court)
      `it was sex discrimination in work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was discrimination against you on the ground of your sex that is unlawful under s 14(1) or (2), 15, 16 or 17 (employment, commission agents, contract workers, partnerships); not worked out in this encoding
      `I suffered detriment for speaking up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were subjected to, or threatened with, a detriment because you complained, brought proceedings, gave information, attended a conference, were a witness, asserted rights or made an allegation under the Act (or because they believed you had or would)
      `the false allegation defence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reason for the detriment was an allegation you made, and it has been proved that the allegation was false and not made in good faith (s 47A(3))
      `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you complained of, asserted or alleged was sex discrimination in work, sexual harassment or harassment on the ground of sex at work, or a hostile workplace environment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the positive duty require the organisation to take measures against this conduct` MEANS `s 47C answer` `the facts`
    WHERE
    `the facts` MEANS Facts WITH `conduct date` IS `date of the conduct`
                                 `org employs` IS `the organisation is an employer`
                                 `org is a PCBU` IS `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking`
                                 `me employee` IS `I am an employee of the organisation`
                                 `me worker` IS `I am a worker in the business or undertaking`
                                 `me seeking` IS `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there`
                                 `actor` IS `who did it`
                                 `connected with my work` IS `it was connected with my being an employee or worker`
                                 `connected with their work` IS `they acted in connection with their own work or business`
                                 `sexual advance` IS `unwelcome sexual advance or request`
                                 `sexual conduct` IS `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature`
                                 `demeaning conduct` IS `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature`
                                 `sex a reason` IS `my sex was one of the reasons`
                                 `reasonable person offence` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate offence`
                                 `in my workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where I work`
                                 `in their workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where they work`
                                 `present` IS `I was there at the time or after`
                                 `reasonable person hostile` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment`
                                 `work discrimination` IS `it was sex discrimination in work`
                                 `victimised` IS `I suffered detriment for speaking up`
                                 `false allegation proved` IS `the false allegation defence is proved`
                                 `raised covered conduct` IS `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace`

@export Which parts of the positive duty (s 47C) cover this conduct?
GIVEN `date of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct happened (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-15)
      `the organisation is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation you are asking about employs people (it may be your employer or someone else's)
      `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is a person conducting a business or undertaking (a PCBU, as in the Work Health and Safety Act 2011)
      `I am an employee of the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed by the organisation
      `I am a worker in the business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carry out work for the organisation's business or undertaking in any capacity (employee, contractor, labour hire, apprentice, volunteer and so on)
      `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were applying or seeking to become an employee of, or a worker in, the organisation
      `who did it` IS A `Who did it` @desc Who did the conduct, as it relates to the organisation: the organisation itself, one of its employees, a worker in its business, one of its agents, or someone else (a customer, client, member of the public, another business's worker)
      `it was connected with my being an employee or worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in connection with your being an employee or a worker (for example at work, at a work event, or because of your work)
      `they acted in connection with their own work or business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who did it is an employee, employer, worker or person conducting a business and did it in connection with being one
      `unwelcome sexual advance or request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was an unwelcome sexual advance, or an unwelcome request for sexual favours, made to you
      `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature towards you, including a statement of a sexual nature made to you or in your presence, spoken or written
      `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature towards you, including a statement made to you or in your presence
      `my sex was one of the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your sex, or a characteristic generally belonging to or assumed of people of your sex, was a reason for the demeaning conduct, even if not the main reason (s 8)
      `a reasonable person would anticipate offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances, would have anticipated the possibility that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated (a judgment for the Commission or court; answer as you expect it to be found)
      `it was in a workplace where I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where you work
      `it was in a workplace where they work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where the person who did it works
      `I was there at the time or after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in that workplace at the same time as the conduct or after it
      `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances (seriousness, repetition, the role or authority of the person), would have anticipated the possibility of the conduct making the workplace offensive, intimidating or humiliating to a person of your sex because of sex or a characteristic of that sex, even as one of several reasons (a judgment for the Commission or court)
      `it was sex discrimination in work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was discrimination against you on the ground of your sex that is unlawful under s 14(1) or (2), 15, 16 or 17 (employment, commission agents, contract workers, partnerships); not worked out in this encoding
      `I suffered detriment for speaking up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were subjected to, or threatened with, a detriment because you complained, brought proceedings, gave information, attended a conference, were a witness, asserted rights or made an allegation under the Act (or because they believed you had or would)
      `the false allegation defence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reason for the detriment was an allegation you made, and it has been proved that the allegation was false and not made in good faith (s 47A(3))
      `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you complained of, asserted or alleged was sex discrimination in work, sexual harassment or harassment on the ground of sex at work, or a hostile workplace environment
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Which parts of the positive duty cover this conduct` MEANS `s 47C paragraphs` `the facts`
    WHERE
    `the facts` MEANS Facts WITH `conduct date` IS `date of the conduct`
                                 `org employs` IS `the organisation is an employer`
                                 `org is a PCBU` IS `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking`
                                 `me employee` IS `I am an employee of the organisation`
                                 `me worker` IS `I am a worker in the business or undertaking`
                                 `me seeking` IS `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there`
                                 `actor` IS `who did it`
                                 `connected with my work` IS `it was connected with my being an employee or worker`
                                 `connected with their work` IS `they acted in connection with their own work or business`
                                 `sexual advance` IS `unwelcome sexual advance or request`
                                 `sexual conduct` IS `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature`
                                 `demeaning conduct` IS `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature`
                                 `sex a reason` IS `my sex was one of the reasons`
                                 `reasonable person offence` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate offence`
                                 `in my workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where I work`
                                 `in their workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where they work`
                                 `present` IS `I was there at the time or after`
                                 `reasonable person hostile` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment`
                                 `work discrimination` IS `it was sex discrimination in work`
                                 `victimised` IS `I suffered detriment for speaking up`
                                 `false allegation proved` IS `the false allegation defence is proved`
                                 `raised covered conduct` IS `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace`

-- s 110: "Except as expressly provided by this Act, nothing in this Act confers on a person any right of action in respect
-- of the doing of an act that is unlawful by reason of a provision of Part II or IIA." AHRC Act s 3(1): "unlawful
-- discrimination" (what a complaint may allege, s 46P) reaches "(c) Part II of the Sex Discrimination Act 1984" -- not
-- Part IIA. s 47B: the President's functions about the duty are in AHRC Act Division 4A (inquiries, compliance notices,
-- undertakings). So a person cannot complain of, or sue for, a breach of s 47C as such; the conduct itself (harassment,
-- a hostile workplace, victimisation, discrimination) is complained of under Part II.
@export Can I bring my own complaint or court claim for a breach of the positive duty itself (s 110; AHRC Act s 3(1))? No: the Commission enforces the duty; the conduct itself can be complained of under Part II.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I bring my own claim for a breach of the positive duty` IS FALSE

§§ `ss 105, 106 -- who else is liable for what was done to me`

-- s 106(1): "where an employee or agent of a person does, in connection with the employment of the employee or with the
-- duties of the agent as an agent: (a) an act that would, if it were done by the person, be unlawful under Division 1 or 2
-- of Part II ...; or (b) an act that is unlawful under Division 3 of Part II; this Act applies in relation to that person
-- as if that person had also done the act." (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply ... if it is established that the person
-- took all reasonable steps to prevent the employee or agent from doing acts of the kind".
-- Division 3 is ss 28A-28M (harassment, hostile workplaces); victimisation is Division 5 and is not in s 106(1).
-- A worker who is neither the organisation's employee nor its agent is outside s 106: NOTHING (the section does not
-- speak; s 105 may). "where" not met, and the s 106(2) "does not apply ... if it is established" -> JUST FALSE.
GIVEN f IS A Facts, `in connection` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106 answer` f `in connection` `reasonable steps` MEANS
    IF NOT `an employee or agent`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF     `in connection`
            AND (   f's `work discrimination`
                 OR `harassment unlawful under s 28B` f
                 OR `subjected to a hostile workplace environment` f)
            AND (NOT `reasonable steps`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `an employee or agent` MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `actor`
            WHEN `an employee of the organisation` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an agent of the organisation` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Is my employer (or the organisation) liable as if it had done what its employee or agent did to me (s 106)?
GIVEN `date of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct happened (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-15)
      `the organisation is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation you are asking about employs people (it may be your employer or someone else's)
      `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is a person conducting a business or undertaking (a PCBU, as in the Work Health and Safety Act 2011)
      `I am an employee of the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed by the organisation
      `I am a worker in the business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carry out work for the organisation's business or undertaking in any capacity (employee, contractor, labour hire, apprentice, volunteer and so on)
      `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were applying or seeking to become an employee of, or a worker in, the organisation
      `who did it` IS A `Who did it` @desc Who did the conduct, as it relates to the organisation: the organisation itself, one of its employees, a worker in its business, one of its agents, or someone else (a customer, client, member of the public, another business's worker)
      `it was connected with my being an employee or worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in connection with your being an employee or a worker (for example at work, at a work event, or because of your work)
      `they acted in connection with their own work or business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who did it is an employee, employer, worker or person conducting a business and did it in connection with being one
      `unwelcome sexual advance or request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was an unwelcome sexual advance, or an unwelcome request for sexual favours, made to you
      `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature towards you, including a statement of a sexual nature made to you or in your presence, spoken or written
      `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature towards you, including a statement made to you or in your presence
      `my sex was one of the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your sex, or a characteristic generally belonging to or assumed of people of your sex, was a reason for the demeaning conduct, even if not the main reason (s 8)
      `a reasonable person would anticipate offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances, would have anticipated the possibility that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated (a judgment for the Commission or court; answer as you expect it to be found)
      `it was in a workplace where I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where you work
      `it was in a workplace where they work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where the person who did it works
      `I was there at the time or after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in that workplace at the same time as the conduct or after it
      `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances (seriousness, repetition, the role or authority of the person), would have anticipated the possibility of the conduct making the workplace offensive, intimidating or humiliating to a person of your sex because of sex or a characteristic of that sex, even as one of several reasons (a judgment for the Commission or court)
      `it was sex discrimination in work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was discrimination against you on the ground of your sex that is unlawful under s 14(1) or (2), 15, 16 or 17 (employment, commission agents, contract workers, partnerships); not worked out in this encoding
      `I suffered detriment for speaking up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were subjected to, or threatened with, a detriment because you complained, brought proceedings, gave information, attended a conference, were a witness, asserted rights or made an allegation under the Act (or because they believed you had or would)
      `the false allegation defence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reason for the detriment was an allegation you made, and it has been proved that the allegation was false and not made in good faith (s 47A(3))
      `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you complained of, asserted or alleged was sex discrimination in work, sexual harassment or harassment on the ground of sex at work, or a hostile workplace environment
      `they acted in connection with their employment or agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee or agent did it in connection with their employment, or with their duties as the organisation's agent
      `the organisation took all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation has established that it took all reasonable steps to prevent its employees or agents from doing acts of that kind (a judgment for the Commission or court; the organisation must show it)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the organisation liable as if it had done what its employee or agent did` MEANS
    `s 106 answer` `the facts` `they acted in connection with their employment or agency` `the organisation took all reasonable steps to prevent it`
    WHERE
    `the facts` MEANS Facts WITH `conduct date` IS `date of the conduct`
                                 `org employs` IS `the organisation is an employer`
                                 `org is a PCBU` IS `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking`
                                 `me employee` IS `I am an employee of the organisation`
                                 `me worker` IS `I am a worker in the business or undertaking`
                                 `me seeking` IS `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there`
                                 `actor` IS `who did it`
                                 `connected with my work` IS `it was connected with my being an employee or worker`
                                 `connected with their work` IS `they acted in connection with their own work or business`
                                 `sexual advance` IS `unwelcome sexual advance or request`
                                 `sexual conduct` IS `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature`
                                 `demeaning conduct` IS `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature`
                                 `sex a reason` IS `my sex was one of the reasons`
                                 `reasonable person offence` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate offence`
                                 `in my workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where I work`
                                 `in their workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where they work`
                                 `present` IS `I was there at the time or after`
                                 `reasonable person hostile` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment`
                                 `work discrimination` IS `it was sex discrimination in work`
                                 `victimised` IS `I suffered detriment for speaking up`
                                 `false allegation proved` IS `the false allegation defence is proved`
                                 `raised covered conduct` IS `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace`

-- s 105: "A person who causes, instructs, induces, aids or permits another person to do an act that is unlawful under
-- Division 1, 2, 3 or 5 of Part II shall, for the purposes of this Act, be taken also to have done the act."
-- Not involved -> JUST FALSE; an unlawful act this encoding can see (work discrimination as an input, s 28B harassment,
-- s 28M, victimisation without the s 47A(3) defence) -> JUST TRUE; harassment outside s 28B (it may be unlawful under ss
-- 28C-28L, not encoded) -> NOTHING; nothing unlawful on these facts -> JUST FALSE.
GIVEN f IS A Facts, `involved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 answer` f `involved` MEANS
    IF NOT `involved` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `an unlawful act this encoding can see`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `harassed` f
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `an unlawful act this encoding can see` MEANS
                f's `work discrimination`
            OR `harassment unlawful under s 28B` f
            OR `subjected to a hostile workplace environment` f
            OR `victimisation unlawful` f

@export Is someone who caused, instructed, induced, aided or permitted what was done to me taken to have done it too (s 105)?
GIVEN `date of the conduct` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct happened (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-15)
      `the organisation is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation you are asking about employs people (it may be your employer or someone else's)
      `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is a person conducting a business or undertaking (a PCBU, as in the Work Health and Safety Act 2011)
      `I am an employee of the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed by the organisation
      `I am a worker in the business or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carry out work for the organisation's business or undertaking in any capacity (employee, contractor, labour hire, apprentice, volunteer and so on)
      `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were applying or seeking to become an employee of, or a worker in, the organisation
      `who did it` IS A `Who did it` @desc Who did the conduct, as it relates to the organisation: the organisation itself, one of its employees, a worker in its business, one of its agents, or someone else (a customer, client, member of the public, another business's worker)
      `it was connected with my being an employee or worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in connection with your being an employee or a worker (for example at work, at a work event, or because of your work)
      `they acted in connection with their own work or business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who did it is an employee, employer, worker or person conducting a business and did it in connection with being one
      `unwelcome sexual advance or request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was an unwelcome sexual advance, or an unwelcome request for sexual favours, made to you
      `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature towards you, including a statement of a sexual nature made to you or in your presence, spoken or written
      `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature towards you, including a statement made to you or in your presence
      `my sex was one of the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your sex, or a characteristic generally belonging to or assumed of people of your sex, was a reason for the demeaning conduct, even if not the main reason (s 8)
      `a reasonable person would anticipate offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances, would have anticipated the possibility that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated (a judgment for the Commission or court; answer as you expect it to be found)
      `it was in a workplace where I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where you work
      `it was in a workplace where they work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct happened in a workplace where the person who did it works
      `I was there at the time or after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in that workplace at the same time as the conduct or after it
      `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances (seriousness, repetition, the role or authority of the person), would have anticipated the possibility of the conduct making the workplace offensive, intimidating or humiliating to a person of your sex because of sex or a characteristic of that sex, even as one of several reasons (a judgment for the Commission or court)
      `it was sex discrimination in work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was discrimination against you on the ground of your sex that is unlawful under s 14(1) or (2), 15, 16 or 17 (employment, commission agents, contract workers, partnerships); not worked out in this encoding
      `I suffered detriment for speaking up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were subjected to, or threatened with, a detriment because you complained, brought proceedings, gave information, attended a conference, were a witness, asserted rights or made an allegation under the Act (or because they believed you had or would)
      `the false allegation defence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reason for the detriment was an allegation you made, and it has been proved that the allegation was false and not made in good faith (s 47A(3))
      `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you complained of, asserted or alleged was sex discrimination in work, sexual harassment or harassment on the ground of sex at work, or a hostile workplace environment
      `someone caused, instructed, induced, aided or permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another person (a manager, the business, a co-worker) caused, instructed, induced, aided or permitted the person who did it to do it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is someone who caused or permitted it taken to have done it too` MEANS
    `s 105 answer` `the facts` `someone caused, instructed, induced, aided or permitted it`
    WHERE
    `the facts` MEANS Facts WITH `conduct date` IS `date of the conduct`
                                 `org employs` IS `the organisation is an employer`
                                 `org is a PCBU` IS `the organisation conducts a business or undertaking`
                                 `me employee` IS `I am an employee of the organisation`
                                 `me worker` IS `I am a worker in the business or undertaking`
                                 `me seeking` IS `I am seeking to become an employee or worker there`
                                 `actor` IS `who did it`
                                 `connected with my work` IS `it was connected with my being an employee or worker`
                                 `connected with their work` IS `they acted in connection with their own work or business`
                                 `sexual advance` IS `unwelcome sexual advance or request`
                                 `sexual conduct` IS `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature`
                                 `demeaning conduct` IS `unwelcome conduct of a demeaning nature`
                                 `sex a reason` IS `my sex was one of the reasons`
                                 `reasonable person offence` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate offence`
                                 `in my workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where I work`
                                 `in their workplace` IS `it was in a workplace where they work`
                                 `present` IS `I was there at the time or after`
                                 `reasonable person hostile` IS `a reasonable person would anticipate a hostile environment`
                                 `work discrimination` IS `it was sex discrimination in work`
                                 `victimised` IS `I suffered detriment for speaking up`
                                 `false allegation proved` IS `the false allegation defence is proved`
                                 `raised covered conduct` IS `what I raised was about work sex discrimination, harassment or a hostile workplace`

§§ `AHRC Act ss 3(1), 46P, 46PH, 46PO, 46PSA -- complaining, time limits and costs`

-- AHRC Act s 46P(1): a written complaint may be lodged alleging acts, omissions or practices that "are unlawful
-- discrimination". (1A): "It must be reasonably arguable that the alleged acts, omissions or practices are unlawful
-- discrimination." (2): by a person aggrieved, by 2 or more, or "(c) by a person or trade union on behalf of one or more
-- other persons aggrieved". (3): "A person who is a class member for a representative complaint is not entitled to lodge
-- a separate complaint in respect of the same subject matter." s 3(1): "unlawful discrimination" reaches "(c) Part II of
-- the Sex Discrimination Act 1984" -- harassment, hostile workplaces and victimisation are all in Part II; Part IIA (the
-- positive duty) is not.
DECLARE `What I allege` IS ONE OF
    `conduct unlawful under Part II (discrimination, harassment, a hostile workplace or victimisation)`
    `only a failure of the positive duty (Part IIA)`

@export Can I lodge a complaint with the Australian Human Rights Commission about this (AHRC Act ss 3(1), 46P)?
GIVEN `what I allege` IS A `What I allege` @desc What the complaint alleges: conduct unlawful under Part II of the Sex Discrimination Act, or only that the employer failed in the positive duty
      `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint is in writing (the Commission must help you put it in writing if you need help)
      `it is reasonably arguable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is reasonably arguable that what you allege is unlawful discrimination
      `I am aggrieved, or a person or union lodges it for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a person aggrieved by it, or a person or trade union is lodging it on your behalf
      `I am a class member of a representative complaint about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are already a class member of a representative complaint about the same subject matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I complain to the Commission` IF
        `alleges unlawful discrimination`
    AND `it is in writing`
    AND `it is reasonably arguable`
    AND `I am aggrieved, or a person or union lodges it for me`
    AND (NOT `I am a class member of a representative complaint about it`)
    WHERE
        `alleges unlawful discrimination` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what I allege`
            WHEN `conduct unlawful under Part II (discrimination, harassment, a hostile workplace or victimisation)` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- AHRC Act s 46PH(1): "The President may terminate a complaint on any of the following grounds: ... (b) the complaint was
-- lodged more than 24 months after the alleged acts, omissions or practices took place". A discretion, not a bar.
@export Could my complaint be ended because I lodged it more than 24 months after the conduct (AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the conduct happened on` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct you complain of took place (the last day, if it went on)
      `I lodge it on` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodge the complaint
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the President end my complaint because it is late` IF
    `I lodge it on` GREATER THAN `months after` `the conduct happened on` 24

-- AHRC Act s 46PO(2): the application to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division
-- 2) "must be made within 60 days after the date of issue of the notice under subsection 46PH(2), or within such further
-- time as the court concerned allows." The further time is the court's to allow: not encoded.
@export By when must I apply to the court after the Commission ends my complaint (AHRC Act s 46PO(2))?
GIVEN `the termination notice was issued on` IS A DATE @desc The date of issue of the President's notice terminating your complaint
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply to the court` MEANS `the termination notice was issued on` PLUS 60

-- AHRC Act s 46PSA(5): "Subject to subsection (6), the applicant must not be ordered by the court to pay costs incurred by
-- another party to the proceedings." (6): "The applicant may be ordered to pay the costs if: (a) the court is satisfied
-- that the applicant instituted the proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause; or (b) the court is satisfied
-- that the applicant's unreasonable act or omission caused the other party to incur the costs; or (c) all of the
-- following apply: (i) the other party is a respondent who was successful in the proceedings; (ii) the respondent does
-- not have a significant power advantage over the applicant; (iii) the respondent does not have significant financial or
-- other resources relative to the applicant."
@export Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs in my court case (AHRC Act s 46PSA(5), (6))?
GIVEN `the court finds I sued vexatiously or without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that you started the proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause
      `the court finds my unreasonable act or omission caused their costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that an unreasonable act or omission of yours caused the other party to incur the costs
      `the respondent won` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other party is a respondent who was successful in the proceedings
      `the respondent has a significant power advantage over me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the respondent has a significant power advantage over you (an employer usually does)
      `the respondent has significantly greater resources than me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the respondent has significant financial or other resources relative to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs` IF
        `the court finds I sued vexatiously or without reasonable cause`
    OR `the court finds my unreasonable act or omission caused their costs`
    OR (    `the respondent won`
        AND (NOT `the respondent has a significant power advantage over me`)
        AND (NOT `the respondent has significantly greater resources than me`))

-- AHRC Act s 46PSA(2): "Subject to subsection (4), if the applicant is successful in proceedings on one or more grounds,
-- the court must order each respondent against whom the applicant is successful to pay the applicant's costs." (4): "If
-- the court is satisfied that the applicant's unreasonable act or omission caused the applicant to incur costs, the court
-- is not required to order the respondent to pay the costs incurred as a result of that act or omission."
DECLARE `My costs if I win` IS ONE OF
    `the respondent must be ordered to pay my costs`
    `the respondent must be ordered to pay my costs, except those my own unreasonable act or omission caused`
    `s 46PSA(2) does not apply: I did not succeed on any ground`

@export If I win in court, must the respondent be ordered to pay my costs (AHRC Act s 46PSA(2), (4))?
GIVEN `I succeeded on at least one ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were successful against the respondent on one or more grounds
      `the court finds my unreasonable act or omission caused some of my costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that an unreasonable act or omission of yours caused you to incur some of your costs
GIVETH A `My costs if I win`
`Must the respondent pay my costs` MEANS
    IF NOT `I succeeded on at least one ground`
    THEN `s 46PSA(2) does not apply: I did not succeed on any ground`
    ELSE IF `the court finds my unreasonable act or omission caused some of my costs`
         THEN `the respondent must be ordered to pay my costs, except those my own unreasonable act or omission caused`
         ELSE `the respondent must be ordered to pay my costs`
